00:05:17,647 --> 00:05:23,647
The man. The legend. The truth.

2
00:10:35,294 --> 00:10:41,294
Tyson is a documentary, drama film directed by James Toback.

3
00:15:52,941 --> 00:15:58,941
Director James Toback takes an unflinching, uncompromising look at the life of
Mike Tyson--almost solely from the perspective of the man himself.

4
00:21:10,588 --> 00:21:16,588
TYSON alternates between the controversial boxer addressing the camera and shots of
the champion's fights to create an arresting picture of the man.

5
00:26:28,235 --> 00:26:34,235
Self, played by Mike Tyson.

6
00:31:45,882 --> 00:31:51,882
Self - Trainer/Manager, played by Cus D'Amato.

7
00:37:03,529 --> 00:37:09,529
Self - Promotor, played by Don King.

8
00:42:21,176 --> 00:42:27,176
Self - Ex-Wife, played by Robin Givens.

9
00:47:38,823 --> 00:47:44,823
Self, played by Mills Lane.

10
00:52:56,470 --> 00:53:02,470
Self, played by Evander Holyfield.

11
00:58:14,117 --> 00:58:20,117
Tyson is a 2008 documentary film about the life of former
undisputed heavyweight world champion boxer Mike Tyson.

12
01:03:31,764 --> 01:03:37,764
It was directed by American filmmaker James Toback and produced by
Nicholas Jarecki, Bob Yari, and NBA player Carmelo Anthony.

13
01:08:49,411 --> 01:08:55,411
The film was publicly screened for the first time at the 2008 Cannes Film Festival
and won the Regard Knockout Award at the Un Certain Regard event.

14
01:14:07,058 --> 01:14:13,058
Tyson was released in a limited on April 24, 2009, then it expanded wide
on May 15, 2009, distributed by Sony Pictures Classics.

15
01:19:24,705 --> 01:19:30,705
The film explores themes of sports, boxer,
biography, sports documentary, box ring.

16
01:24:42,352 --> 01:24:48,352
The tone is emotional.
